      'The 1998 Nintendo 64 game The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time was long seen as the best game ever made, and already got a version on the Nintendo 3DS in 2011. At release the game stood out because it took the Zelda series, which until then was playable in two dimensions, into three dimensions. It also offered a large, lively feeling game world for the time, with diverse regions and timeless puzzles.',
      'Update on the live action film. There was a little more talk about the upcoming live action The Legend of Zelda film during the Direct, but the expected trailer unfortunately stayed away. Shigeru Miyamoto did reconfirm the 30 April release date, and “revealed” that the film will be called The Legend of Zelda. Apparently that was a reveal.',
